 "notes": [
  "Written 2026-10-29 from the build's own definitions only (runs/a24/zflx/r1/exec: ui_flow_bd6d62a1\u2026json.md via tools/a24_map_helper.py, workflow_*.md, system_*.md, data_types.txt, slices_*.md), before any workflow of the build was run and before any output was opened.",
  "UI flow: one page (CardDemoPage) whose cards are shown by ${screen}: SIGNON, MAIN_MENU, ADMIN_MENU, ACCOUNT_SEARCH/ACCOUNT_DETAILS, BILL_PAYMENT, EXIT. Each legacy map corresponds to one card; navigation is the ui.screen value the action's workflow returns.",
  "Response paths: the four workflows have no OUTPUT slice. Each workflow's own description and the register (assumptions.md #3) state the END payload is ${ui}, and the UI flow reads ${screen}, ${signonMessage} \u2026 at the top level. So the map reads top-level paths (screen, signonMessage, acct.* \u2026). The END payload itself cannot be read back with the zflx tools; if a workflow returned the whole data instead, its values would sit under ui.* and these paths would be empty. That is the operator's written choice; the browser subset (H18) checks what the page shows.",
  "Start: the page's own action initSignon (ui_signon type init) runs when the page opens; both CC00 and CB00 open the UI flow on the sign-on card (the flow has no other entry).",
  "Not shown as separate page elements, so not mapped (missing on the page): ACSFNAM/ACSMNAM/ACSLNAM (one combined customerName), ACSADL1/ACSADL2/ACSCITY/ACSSTTE/ACSCTRY/ACSZIPC (one combined address), ACSPHN1/ACSPHN2 (one combined phones), AADDGRP (groupId not on the page), INFOMSG (no info line), OPTN011 (the option list has 10 lines).",
  "OPTN001-OPTN010: the lines of the page's constant text MainMenuOptions.",
  "Stores: the build's five stores keep the CONTRACT-UI field names and types (data_types.txt): identity field map, no text fields. No loader workflows in the build: operator loaders via make-loader.",
  "Not reachable (no button): PF5 everywhere; PF4 except on bill payment."
 ],
